<div class="bhd-page__keypoints" aria-label="Clinical hydration principles">
  <div><strong>Assess the cause</strong><span>Low intake, gastrointestinal loss, fever, medication, kidney function and other conditions can require different responses.</span></div>
  <div><strong>Choose the right route</strong><span>Oral intake is appropriate only when the person can drink safely and the clinical situation supports it.</span></div>
  <div><strong>Follow the authorized use</strong><span>Best Hydrate is a licensed Canadian natural health product, but its NPN does not authorize every proposed medical application.</span></div>
